<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawAcceptance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawAcceptance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Removes a Manager's own `ProposalAcceptance`, only while the `SlotProposal` has fewer than 3 acceptances." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawAcceptance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "WithdrawAcceptance" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawAcceptance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#UseCase> <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawAcceptance> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#definedIn> "[slot-negotiation](../.kiro/specs/slot-negotiation/design.md)" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawProposal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawProposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sets a `SlotProposal`'s status to Withdrawn (creator only, pre-confirmation)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawProposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "WithdrawProposal" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawProposal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#UseCase> <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#WithdrawProposal> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#definedIn> "[slot-negotiation](../.kiro/specs/slot-negotiation/design.md)" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_10> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`CandidateReadiness`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_10> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "`Ready` requires an active original Booking and one Completed Booking Appointment for every current derived Candidate Requirement across that original Booking and its non-cancelled recovery Bookings. Expected, Checked in, and No-show are outstanding; cancelled Booking Appointments and non-required Appointment Types are excluded. No active original Booking, a temporarily unassigned Employee Group, or a requirement snapshot mismatch is explicitly not ready. See [Issue #91 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-employee-group-requirements-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_11> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "Recovery Booking" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_11> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "A recovery Invite and Booking cover only current requirements whose latest non-cancelled Booking Appointment is No-show and for which no Completed attempt exists. Completed appointments are never recreated or charged capacity again. A recovery Booking becomes Concluded when all its appointments are Completed or No-show; repeated No-show can then create another recovery. A No-show correction is rejected while a later pending or non-cancelled recovery exists. See [Issue #91 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-employee-group-requirements-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_12> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`SlotWindow`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_12> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "Every window is exactly 4 hours; only its `date` and `startTime` are stored, so a proposal and the `ConfirmedSlot` derived from it can never disagree about duration. See [Plan 02](detailed-implementations/2026-09-03-joint-booking/02-domain-appointment-types.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_13> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`StaffIdentity`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_13> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "Exactly one row per authenticated staff identity, keyed by `staffUserId`, with `staffId` unique across the table. Both fields are immutable in practice: the provider never reissues `staffUserId` for the same person and HR never changes a `StaffId`. An authenticated request whose pair is not already cached upserts it, so the mirror converges from tokens alone, without a directory query; `lastSeenAt` is refreshed on those writes only and is therefore approximate. `displayName` refreshes on the same cache-miss cadence as `lastSeenAt` and carries the same approximateness — it can lag a rename in the identity provider until the next sign-in — and, unlike `staffId`, its absence never blocks anything: a null `displayName` falls back to `staffId` or an opaque identifier wherever a staff identity is shown. A token with no `StaffId` claim, or one carrying a malformed value, records no row and is refused by every staff-authorized endpoint even where a `StaffAccessProfile` exists, since a staff identity JointBooking cannot name must not appear in an `AuditLog`. See [StaffId claim design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-07-staff-id-claim-design.md) and [Staff identity display name design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-15-staff-identity-display-name-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_1> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`StaffAccessProfile`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_1> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "Admin is exclusive and has no `AppointmentType`; Coordinator may combine with Manager and/or AppointmentStaff but never Admin; Manager and AppointmentStaff share the profile's one `AppointmentType` scope. Admin receives no candidate data. Each `AppointmentType` has at most one current Manager profile, while any number of AppointmentStaff profiles may share it. Manager or AppointmentStaff may transiently carry a null scope immediately after an identity-provider role sync and before an Admin assigns the appointment type; that shape is valid but grants no capabilities until scope is set. See [Issue #71 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-scoped-multi-role-authorization-design.md) and [IdP-sourced roles design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-10-idp-sourced-staff-roles-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_2> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`ConfirmedSlot`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_2> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "A `SlotProposal` becomes a `ConfirmedSlot` only once all 3 Managers (one per `AppointmentType`) have accepted it, each supplying their own headcount. An Admin or Coordinator may instead bulk-import a `ConfirmedSlot` directly, with `proposalId` left null; either way, once created it behaves identically for every later operation. See [Area B](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/b-slot-negotiation.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_3> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`ProposalAcceptance`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_3> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "While its `SlotProposal` remains `Open`, the manager recorded in `managerUserId` may replace their own positive `headcount` without withdrawing the acceptance. A different manager cannot read or change that value. See [Area B](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/b-slot-negotiation.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_4> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`SlotCapacity`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_4> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "`remainingCapacity` must never go below 0 or above the current `totalHeadcount` for that `AppointmentType` on that `ConfirmedSlot`. While the slot remains `Active`, its current Manager may replace `totalHeadcount` with a positive total no lower than the active-booking count, changing `remainingCapacity` by the same delta. Every read-check-write is one atomic, row-locked transaction. This is the mechanism behind \"no overbooking.\" See [Area G](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/g-capacity-concurrency-rules.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_5> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`Invite`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_5> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "Every `Invite` offers exactly 3 `InviteOption`s, each a `ConfirmedSlot` with spare `SlotCapacity` in every snapshotted `InviteRequirement`. An initial Invite snapshots every current derived `CandidateRequirement`; a recovery Invite snapshots only recoverable outstanding no-show types and identifies the active original Booking. A group-changing edit supersedes a pending initial Invite, while a Coordinator may explicitly cancel a recovery Invite. See [Area D](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/d-invite-engine.md) and [Issue #91 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-employee-group-requirements-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_6> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`Booking`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_6> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "Cancelling a `ConfirmedSlot` voids every `Booking` against it, frees its `SlotCapacity`, and triggers a fresh `Invite` for each affected `Candidate`. See [Area F](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/f-cancellation-reschedule.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_7> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`BookingAppointment`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_7> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "A booking creates exactly one per candidate requirement in the same transaction, unique by (`Booking`, `AppointmentType`). Its normal lifecycle is `Expected` → `CheckedIn` → `Completed` or `Expected` → `NoShow`; only the bounded corrections `CheckedIn` → `Expected`, `Completed` → `CheckedIn`, and `NoShow` → `Expected` are permitted. A same-status submission is idempotent. Check-in is limited to the slot's head-office date, no-show is permitted only after its four-hour window, and every real transition is versioned and audited. Active bookings and active slots are required for mutation. See [Issue #26 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-07-booking-appointment-workspace-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_8> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`CandidateRequirement`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_8> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "The requirement set cannot change while the candidate has an active original `Booking`; name and email corrections and set-equivalent Employee Group changes remain permitted. Outside a legacy reconciliation window, requirements are derived only from the Candidate's active `EmployeeGroup` and are never caller-selected. Cancellation makes old `BookingAppointment` records read-only and a replacement initial booking snapshots the then-current set. See [Issue #26 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-07-booking-appointment-workspace-design.md) and [Issue #91 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-employee-group-requirements-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_9> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantLabel> "`EmployeeGroup`" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_invariant_9> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#invariantText> "The initial five groups and their mappings to the existing three fixed Appointment Types are deterministic, change-controlled reference data. Every active group has at least one known, non-duplicated mapping. Group codes are immutable, unique, canonical uppercase snake case, and accepted case-insensitively at input boundaries. Runtime editing and dynamic Appointment Types are outside Issue #91. See [Issue #91 design](superpowers/specs/2026-09-09-employee-group-requirements-design.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_meta> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#preamble> "<!-- GENERATED FROM docs/ontology.ttl. Edit that file, not this one, then run\n     `node --experimental-strip-types scripts/build-ontology.ts`. -->\n\n> **AI instructions:** Read this file in full before starting any task that touches domain\n> concepts. To change it, edit `docs/ontology.ttl` and run\n> `node --experimental-strip-types scripts/build-ontology.ts`. This file must never lag behind the\n> specs and plan docs. See [AGENTS.md](../AGENTS.md) for the enforcement mechanism.\n\nThis is derived from the entities and rules already established in\n[docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-joint-booking-design.md](superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-joint-booking-design.md)\nand [docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/)\n(the entity relationship diagram in Area L in particular), and refined by the executable plan set in\n[docs/detailed-implementations/2026-09-03-joint-booking/](detailed-implementations/2026-09-03-joint-booking/00-overview.md), which pins the previously prose-only status vocabularies\ndown to named enums. Later designs add their vocabulary here before their plan documents consume it;\nthe Issue #26 appointment-workspace design is the source for `BookingAppointment` and its lifecycle.\nThis file is the single canonical reference for exact naming." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_meta> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#projectName> "JointBooking" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_section_Enums> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#sectionOutro> "The status vocabularies above were originally recorded in the Area files as prose multi-word phrases\n(\"Not yet invited\", \"No response - needs follow-up\"). Those phrases remain the display wording; the\nenum members here are the canonical identifiers the code and the plan documents use. The mapping is\none-to-one and is set out in [Plan 04](detailed-implementations/2026-09-03-joint-booking/04-domain-candidates-invites.md)." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#_section_Use_Cases> <https://jointbooking.internal/ontology-kit#sectionIntro> "Application-layer operations named consistently across the Kiro specs under\n[docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/](superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-joint-booking/)\nand [.kiro/specs/](../.kiro/specs/). Listed here because they're backticked in those design docs\nand cross-referenced between specs — not because every use case needs an ontology entry; only\nthese are named enough times elsewhere that inconsistent spelling would actually cause confusion." <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#assigned_to> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
<https://jointbooking.internal/ontology#assigned_to> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "assigned to" <urn:division-ontology:source:jamiemitchellconsultants%2FJointBooking:6957928a6c9054372dda915b359f63b73969ebee> .
